      "safety_netting": "Seek immediate help by calling 999 or going to A&E if you experience: thoughts of harming yourself or your babies with a plan or intent, hearing voices or seeing things that aren't there, feeling unable to care for your babies' basic needs, or feeling completely overwhelmed and unable to cope. Contact the GP surgery urgently (same day or next day) if: your mood suddenly worsens significantly, you develop new concerning thoughts about yourself or the babies, you're unable to sleep at all even when babies are sleeping, you stop eating or drinking, or you feel your symptoms are rapidly getting worse. Call 111 or the crisis helpline if you're struggling outside of surgery hours and need support. Contact the surgery for a routine appointment within 1-2 weeks if: you're not seeing any improvement in your symptoms, you're experiencing side effects from medication that are concerning you, or you have questions about your treatment plan. Remember, you can also contact your health visitor at any time for support - they are there to help, not to judge. Keep the Samaritans number saved in your phone (116 123) - they're available 24/7 if you need someone to talk to. If your partner or family members are concerned about you, please listen to them and seek help. It's important to know that asking for help is a sign of strength and good parenting, not weakness. We're here to support you through this, and you don't have to manage alone.",
