      "safety_netting": "Seek immediate medical attention by calling 999 or going to A&E if you experience: severe chest pain or pressure, difficulty breathing or shortness of breath, collapse or loss of consciousness, seizure or fit, severe headache with neck stiffness, confusion or disorientation, thoughts of harming yourself or suicide. Contact the GP surgery urgently (same day) if: palpitations become more frequent or severe, anxiety becomes unmanageable or you have panic attacks lasting more than 30 minutes, you feel unable to cope or have thoughts of self-harm, you develop new symptoms like severe abdominal pain or blood in urine. Book a routine appointment if: symptoms aren't improving after one week, sleep problems persist beyond two weeks, you'd like to discuss mental health support or counseling, you have questions about the test results, you'd like support talking to your mum or other family members. Remember you can also contact FRANK (0300 123 6600) 24/7 for confidential advice about drugs, or text FRANK to 82111. If you're feeling anxious or need someone to talk to, you can call Childline (0800 1111) or The Mix (0808 808 4994) anytime - they're confidential and won't tell your mum. Out of hours, if you're concerned but it's not an emergency, call NHS 111 for advice.",
