    "management_overview": "**Immediate Actions**\n- IV access and fluid resuscitation if systemically unwell\n- Urgent joint aspiration (send for microscopy, culture, crystal analysis)\n- Blood cultures if febrile\n- Analgesia (titrated to pain)\n- Nil by mouth pending surgical intervention\n- Diabetic management (sliding scale insulin if needed)\n- Perform sepsis 6 but omit antibiotics until aspirate has been taken. If clinically septic, however, give antibiotics as soon as possible.\n\n**Antibiotics**\n- Start empirical IV antibiotics after cultures taken\n- Follow local microbiology guidelines\n- Typically flucloxacillin + gentamicin or ceftriaxone\n- Adjust based on culture results\n\n**Surgical Management**\n- Urgent arthroscopic washout (or open if required)\n- Multiple samples for microbiology\n- Thorough lavage\n- Consider repeat washout if inadequate response\n\n**Post-operative Care**\n- Continue IV antibiotics\n- Regular monitoring of inflammatory markers\n- Early physiotherapy and mobilization\n- Diabetic control optimization\n\n**Multidisciplinary Input**\n- Microbiology input for antibiotic management\n- Diabetic team involvement\n- Physiotherapy\n- Infectious disease consultation if complex\n\n**Discharge Planning**\n- Conversion to oral antibiotics when appropriate\n- Outpatient follow-up\n- Glycemic control education",
