ding on fixation method that accommodates soft tissue needs\n4. Determining appropriate soft tissue reconstruction (likely requiring flap coverage)\n5. Scheduling combined orthoplastic procedure\n\nThe evidence shows that early soft tissue coverage (within 72 hours) significantly reduces infection rates and improves outcomes in open tibial fractures. The British Association of Plastic, Reconstructive and Aesthetic Surgeons (BAPRAS) guidelines emphasize this combined approach as the standard of care for these injuries.",
