        "answer": "I would use the SPIKES protocol to structure my approach:\n\n**Setting:** I would ensure we have a private, quiet room with comfortable seating and no interruptions. I would silence my phone/pager and ensure adequate time is allocated for the consultation.\n\n**Perception:** I would begin by asking Mr. Wilson what he understands about his condition: \"What's your understanding of the shoulder pain you've been experiencing?\"\n\n**Invitation:** I would assess how much information he wants: \"I have your scan results - would you like me to explain them in detail?\"\n\n**Knowledge:** I would deliver the information clearly and honestly:\n\"The scans show an area of bone damage in your upper arm near the shoulder. The appearance suggests this could be a tumor in the bone. At this stage, we don't know exactly what type of tumor this is, but we need to investigate further.\"\n\n**Empathy:** I would acknowledge his emotional response:\n\"I understand this is unexpected and concerning news. It's completely normal to feel shocked or upset.\"\n\n**Summarize and Strategy:** I would outline next steps:\n\"We need to perform a biopsy to determine exactly what type of tumor this is. I'll refer you to our regional bone tumor unit where specialists will coordinate your care. Do you have any questions about what happens next?\"\n\nI would also check if Mr. Wilson would like someone to be with him, offer to call a family member, and provide written information about the suspected diagnosis and next steps.",
