    "breaking_bad_news_framework": "**Setting:** Ensure a private, quiet consultation room with no interruptions. Arrange seating so you are at the same level as Mr. Wilson, without barriers between you. Allocate sufficient time for the consultation and ensure your pager is on silent.\n\n**Perception:** Begin by exploring Mr. Wilson's understanding of his condition. \"Mr. Wilson, what is your understanding of why you've been experiencing pain in your shoulder?\"\n\n**Invitation:** Assess how much information Mr. Wilson wants to know. \"I have the results of your scans. Would you like me to go through them in detail with you?\"\n\n**Knowledge:** Deliver the information clearly and simply, avoiding jargon.\n\"The scans show an area of bone damage in your upper arm near the shoulder. The appearance is concerning as it shows features that could indicate a tumor in the bone. I want to be clear that we don't know for certain what type of tumor this is yet, but we need to investigate further.\"\n\n**Empathy:** Acknowledge and validate Mr. Wilson's emotional response.\n\"I understand this must be very unexpected and concerning news. It's completely normal to feel shocked or upset when hearing something like this.\"\n\n**Summarize and Strategy:** Outline the next steps clearly.\n\"Let me explain what happens next. We need to perform a biopsy, which is a procedure to take a small sample of the affected bone. This will help us determine exactly what type of tumor this is. I'll refer you to our regional bone tumor unit where specialists will coordinate your care. Do you have any questions about what I've explained or what happens next?\"",
