    "management_overview": "**Immediate Management:**\n- PRICE (Protection, Rest, Ice, Compression, Elevation)\n- Adequate analgesia (consider regional nerve block)\n- Non-weight-bearing status\n- Temporary splinting in neutral position\n\n**Surgical Planning:**\n- NBM status if surgery anticipated\n- Urgent CT scan for surgical planning\n- Consent for ORIF vs primary arthrodesis\n- Mark surgical site\n- Prophylactic antibiotics as per local protocol\n- VTE risk assessment and prophylaxis\n\n**Operative Management Options:**\n1. Stable non-displaced injuries: cast immobilization with close follow-up\n2. Unstable or displaced injuries:\n   - ORIF with screws/plates\n   - Primary arthrodesis for severely comminuted injuries\n   - Temporary bridge plating or external fixation for severe soft tissue compromise\n\n**Post-operative Care:**\n- Non-weight-bearing for 6-12 weeks\n- Regular wound checks\n- Staged soft tissue procedures if needed\n- Early physiotherapy for non-operative limb\n\n**Follow-up:**\n- Regular radiographic assessment\n- Graduated weight-bearing protocol\n- Consideration of orthotic support\n- Return to work/sport assessment",
