age grip strength: 60-80% of contralateral side\n- Range of motion: 70-80% of normal\n- Return to previous occupation: 50-75%\n- Persistent pain: 25-60%\n\nOverall, the evidence suggests that despite optimal management, many patients have persistent symptoms and functional limitations following perilunate dislocations. Early diagnosis, anatomic reduction, stable fixation, and appropriate rehabilitation are key to optimizing outcomes.",
