    "breaking_bad_news_framework": "The SPIES-R framework is a structured clinical tool used to manage ethical dilemmas, professional misconduct, or patient safety concerns. It ensures a logical progression from fact-finding to personal growth.\n\n**The SPIES-R Framework**\n\n**Seek Information**: Establish the facts before acting. This involves reviewing clinical documentation (patient notes/charts) and holding objective discussions with those involved to gather multiple perspectives.\n\n**Patient Safety**: This is the non-negotiable priority. You must take immediate, practical steps to neutralize any threat of harm to patients, such as intervening in an unsafe procedure or correcting a medical error.\n\n**Initiative**: Demonstrate leadership by taking active steps to resolve the immediate problem. This involves deciding on a course of action rather than waiting for others to intervene.\n\n**Escalate**: Recognize the limits of your authority. Formally report the incident to a direct senior (Registrar, Consultant, or Clinical Lead) and ensure appropriate organizational channels are notified.\n\n**Support**: Acknowledge the human element. Offer collegiate support to those involved and signpost them to professional wellbeing services, such as Occupational Health, the BMA, or their GP.\n\n**Reflect**: Close the loop by documenting the event in your professional portfolio (e.g., ISCP or e-Portfolio). Use the experience to identify learning points and improve future practice.",
