    "interview_questions": [
      {
        "answer": "I would use the SBAR (Situation, Background, Assessment, Recommendation) framework to ensure clear, concise communication:\n\n**Situation:**\n- Introduce myself clearly: \"Hello, this is Dr. [Name], ST3 in Orthopaedics\"\n- State the purpose immediately: \"I'm calling about an urgent case requiring your input for an external fixator application\"\n- Emphasize time-critical nature: \"The patient has developing neurovascular compromise\"\n\n**Background:**\n- Patient demographics: \"Mr. Thompson, 42-year-old male, construction worker\"\n- Mechanism: \"Fall from height at work\"\n- Injury: \"Closed comminuted distal tibia fracture with significant displacement\"\n- Relevant past history: \"No significant past medical history/medications\"\n\n**Assessment:**\n- Current status: \"I've attempted closed reduction under sedation but couldn't achieve adequate alignment\"\n- Neurovascular status: \"Patient now has decreased sensation in first web space, weak great toe dorsiflexion, cooler foot with delayed capillary refill\"\n- Imaging findings: \"X-rays show comminuted fracture with significant displacement and CT confirms articular involvement\"\n- My interpretation: \"This represents anterior tibial nerve compromise and possible vascular compromise requiring urgent intervention\"\n\n**Recommendation:**\n- Clear request: \"I believe an external fixator is indicated urgently\"\n- Acknowledge limitations: \"I'm not yet competent to perform this independently\"\n- Proposed plan: \"I've prepared the patient, obtained consent, and organized theater staff and equipment\"\n- Direct question: \"Could you please come in to supervise/assist with the external fixator application?\"\n\nI would document this conversation contemporaneously in the patient's notes, including the time of the call, the information conveyed, the consultant's response, and the agreed plan.",
        "question": "How would you structure your phone call to the consultant?"
