        "answer": "**Documentation of Consultant Discussion:**\n\nI would document the discussion comprehensively in the patient's medical record as follows:\n\n```\nDate: [Date]\nTime: 02:30\n\nDiscussion with Mr./Ms. [Consultant Name], Consultant Orthopaedic Surgeon, regarding Mr. Robert Thompson (DOB: [DOB], Hospital No: [Number])\n\nInformation conveyed:\n- Patient sustained closed comminuted distal tibia fracture following fall from height\n- Failed closed reduction under sedation\n- Developing neurovascular compromise: decreased sensation in first web space, weak great toe dorsiflexion, cooler foot with delayed capillary refill\n- Need for urgent external fixation\n- My lack of independent competence with external fixator application\n\nConsultant's advice:\n- [Document exact advice given]\n- [Document any specific technical instructions provided]\n\nAgreed plan:\n- Consultant to attend to supervise external fixator application\n- Expected arrival time: [Time]\n- Theater team notified and equipment prepared\n- Patient to be monitored closely for worsening neurovascular status while awaiting consultant arrival\n- [Any other agreed actions]\n\nDr. [My Name]\nST3 Orthopaedics\nGMC: [Number]\n```\n\nI would ensure this documentation is:\n\n**Contemporaneous:** Written at the time of or immediately after the conversation\n\n**Comprehensive:** Including all relevant clinical information shared, advice received, and decisions made\n\n**Clear:** Using precise language without ambiguity about the plan\n\n**Factual:** Avoiding subjective statements or blame\n\n**Identifiable:** Including names, roles, and GMC numbers of all involved\n\n**Timed:** With exact times of conversation and expected actions\n\nThis documentation serves multiple purposes:\n- Creates a clear record of clinical decision-making\n- Establishes the escalation of care pathway\n- Demonstrates appropriate seeking of help when needed\n- Provides continuity of care information\n- Fulfills medico-legal requirements\n- Reflects good practice as per GMC guidance on record-keeping",
