emand athletes\n   - Quadriceps tendon: Emerging option with good outcomes and less donor site morbidity\n   - Patient preference after discussion of pros/cons\n\n**For this specific patient:**\nGiven her age, activity level, and sport type, I would recommend ACL reconstruction after discussing options. As a semi-professional footballer with likely aspirations to continue at a high level, non-operative management carries significant risk of instability during pivoting movements and potential for secondary meniscal/chondral damage. The specific graft choice would be discussed with the patient after reviewing pros and cons of each option, with patellar tendon or hamstring autograft being most appropriate for a young athlete.",
