        "answer": "I would approach this difficult conversation using the SPIKES protocol:\n\n**Setting:** I would find a private room where Mrs. Johnson can sit comfortably, ensuring we won't be interrupted. I would invite her daughter to join us if Mrs. Johnson wishes.\n\n**Perception:** I would begin by asking what Mrs. Johnson understands about the current situation and if she's aware of any delays.\n\n**Invitation:** I would prepare her for the news: \"I need to discuss something important about your surgery today.\"\n\n**Knowledge:** I would clearly explain the situation: \"I'm very sorry, but we need to reschedule your knee replacement. The previous operation has run significantly over time, and your consultant has been called to assist with an emergency trauma case.\"\n\n**Empathy:** I would acknowledge her feelings: \"I understand this is extremely disappointing, especially after your mental preparation and your daughter traveling to help you. Your frustration is completely understandable.\"\n\n**Summarize:** I would outline next steps: \"I'll personally ensure you're prioritized on the next available list, ideally within 1-2 weeks. I'll arrange for a letter explaining the cancellation for your employer if needed. We'll also ensure your pre-operative assessments remain valid for the rescheduled date.\"\n\nThroughout the conversation, I would maintain eye contact, use an empathetic tone, and give Mrs. Johnson time to process the information and express her feelings.",
