    "breaking_bad_news_framework": "**Setting:** Find a quiet, private room where you can speak with Mrs. Johnson without interruptions. Ensure she is comfortable and sitting down. Consider allowing her daughter to be present if Mrs. Johnson wishes.\n\n**Perception:** Begin by assessing Mrs. Johnson's current understanding and expectations. \"How has your experience been so far today, Mrs. Johnson? Have you been informed about any potential timing issues?\"\n\n**Invitation:** Prepare Mrs. Johnson for the news. \"I need to discuss something important with you regarding your scheduled surgery today. Is it okay if we talk about this now?\"\n\n**Knowledge:** Deliver the information clearly and directly. \"I'm very sorry to inform you that we will need to reschedule your knee replacement surgery. The previous operation has taken significantly longer than anticipated, and unfortunately, your consultant has been called to assist with an emergency trauma case. This means we cannot proceed with your surgery today as planned.\"\n\n**Empathy:** Acknowledge the impact and validate her feelings. \"I understand this is extremely disappointing news, especially after you've prepared yourself mentally and made arrangements with your daughter travelling from Scotland. I recognize this disruption is frustrating and upsetting, and your feelings are completely valid.\"\n\n**Summarize:** Outline the next steps clearly. \"Here's what will happen next: I will personally discuss with the consultant to try to ensure that you're prioritized on the next available list, ideally within the next 1-2 weeks. I can provide a letter explaining the cancellation for your employer if needed. Do you have any questions about what happens now or concerns I can address?\"",
