      {
        "answer": "I would consent Mrs. Wilson for revision hip surgery using the following structured approach:\n\n**Establish capacity:** First, I would ensure Mrs. Wilson has capacity to make decisions about her treatment according to the Mental Capacity Act 2005. This involves assessing if she can understand, retain, and weigh information, and communicate her decision.\n\n**Provide information:** I would explain in clear, non-technical language:\n\n1. **The diagnosis:** Aseptic loosening of the acetabular component\n\n2. **The proposed procedure:** Revision hip arthroplasty, including:\n   - Removal of loose components\n   - Possible bone grafting\n   - Insertion of new components\n   - Potential need to revise femoral component\n\n3. **Benefits:**\n   - Pain relief\n   - Improved mobility and function\n   - Prevention of further bone damage\n\n4. **Risks:**\n   - General surgical risks (infection 1-2%, bleeding, DVT/PE 1-5%)\n   - Specific risks of revision surgery:\n     - Higher infection rate (2-4%)\n     - Dislocation (5-10%)\n     - Leg length discrepancy\n     - Nerve injury (1%)\n     - Periprosthetic fracture (3-5%)\n     - Potential need for further revision\n\n5. **Recovery expectations:**\n   - Longer hospital stay (5-7 days)\n   - Extended rehabilitation period\n   - Possible blood transfusion\n   - Slower return to function\n\n6. **Alternatives:**\n   - Conservative management with analgesia and mobility aids\n   - Different types of revision implants\n\n**Check understanding:** I would ask Mrs. Wilson to explain back her understanding of the procedure, risks, and benefits to ensure comprehension.\n\n**Document discussion:** I would document the consent discussion in detail in the medical records.\n\n**Complete consent form:** I would use **Consent Form 1** (for adults with capacity) as per Department of Health guidance, ensuring all discussed risks and benefits are documented.\n\n**Provide written information:** I would provide an information leaflet about revision hip surgery for Mrs. Wilson to review at home.\n\n**Allow time for consideration:** I would offer Mrs. Wilson time to consider her options and discuss with family before making a final decision.\n\n**Address specific concerns:** I would ensure any specific concerns raised by Mrs. Wilson or her son are addressed and documented.",
