        "answer": "If Mr. Wilson threatens to make a formal complaint, I would handle the situation as follows:\n\n**Remain calm and professional:** I would maintain a composed demeanor and avoid becoming defensive or dismissive.\n\n**Listen actively:** I would allow Mr. Wilson to express his concerns fully without interruption, demonstrating that I take his concerns seriously.\n\n**Acknowledge his right to complain:** I would validate his right to raise concerns:\n\"Mr. Wilson, I understand your concerns, and you absolutely have the right to make a formal complaint if you feel that's necessary.\"\n\n**Provide information about the complaints process:** I would explain:\n- How to access the hospital's PALS (Patient Advice and Liaison Service)\n- The formal complaints procedure\n- Timeframes for responses\n- His right to escalate to the Parliamentary and Health Service Ombudsman if unsatisfied\n\n**Attempt resolution:** I would try to address his immediate concerns:\n\"Before you proceed with a formal complaint, I'd like to understand exactly what your concerns are and see if we can address them today. What specific aspects of your mother's care are you most concerned about?\"\n\n**Be transparent:** I would provide honest explanations about what happened, avoiding defensive language or attributing blame.\n\n**Involve senior colleagues:** If appropriate, I would offer to arrange a meeting with a consultant or the clinical director:\n\"Would it be helpful to discuss your concerns with my consultant? They can provide more information about your mother's treatment and the complication.\"\n\n**Document meticulously:** Following the conversation, I would document all concerns raised and my responses in the medical record.\n\n**Reflect on practice:** I would consider whether there are legitimate learning points from his concerns, regardless of whether a formal complaint is made.\n\n**Seek support:** I would discuss the case with my educational supervisor and consider whether I need additional support from defense organizations or senior colleagues.\n\n**Follow up:** I would ensure appropriate follow-up of any issues raised, even if a formal complaint is made.\n\nThroughout this process, I would maintain focus on Mrs. Wilson's ongoing care needs while addressing Mr. Wilson's concerns professionally and compassionately, in line with GMC guidance on handling complaints.",
