d joint involvement\n   - Hawkins classification\n\n2. **Patient Factors:**\n   - Young, high-demand athlete with significant functional requirements\n   - Expectations regarding return to sport\n   - Compliance with rehabilitation protocols\n\n3. **Timing:**\n   - Urgent reduction reduces AVN risk\n   - May need to balance against soft tissue swelling\n\n4. **Associated Injuries:**\n   - Presence of ankle mortise disruption, other tarsal fractures, or ligamentous injuries\n\n5. **Long-term Considerations:**\n   - Risk of post-traumatic arthritis\n   - Potential need for future procedures (arthrodesis, arthroplasty)\n   - Career implications for a semi-professional athlete",
