        "answer": "**Rehabilitation Protocol for Proximal Humerus Fracture:**\n\n**Phase 1: Protection Phase (0-3 weeks)**\n\n- Immobilization in sling (duration based on treatment method and stability)\n- Early finger, wrist, and elbow ROM exercises\n- Pendulum exercises starting at 7-10 days (conservative) or 2-3 days (post-surgical)\n- Pain and edema control (ice, elevation)\n- Patient education on posture and positioning\n- Scapular setting exercises\n\n**Phase 2: Early Motion Phase (3-6 weeks)**\n\n- Progressive passive ROM exercises\n- Active-assisted ROM as tolerated\n- Continue pendulum exercises\n- Isometric rotator cuff exercises (submaximal)\n- Scapular stabilization exercises\n- Wean from sling (typically by week 4-6)\n\n**Phase 3: Intermediate Phase (6-12 weeks)**\n\n- Full active ROM exercises\n- Progressive rotator cuff strengthening\n- Functional movement patterns\n- Proprioceptive training\n- Light functional activities\n\n**Phase 4: Advanced Strengthening (12+ weeks)**\n\n- Progressive resistance training\n- Overhead activities\n- Sport or occupation-specific training\n- Endurance training\n\n",
