        "answer": "Thomas would require a **Consent Form 2**, which is specifically designed for patients under 18 years of age who are not Gillick competent or where parental consent is being obtained alongside the child's assent.\n\nThis form includes:\n- Details of the proposed procedure (elbow arthroscopy for removal of loose bodies)\n- Benefits and risks of the procedure\n- Alternative treatment options\n- Space for the parent/guardian's signature (Thomas's father in this case)\n- Space for the healthcare professional's signature\n- Documentation of Thomas's involvement in the discussion\n\nWhile Thomas at 15 years old may potentially be Gillick competent depending on his understanding and maturity, in most cases involving minors undergoing surgical procedures, Form 2 is used with parental consent. If Thomas were deemed Gillick competent and wished to consent himself, this would need careful assessment and documentation.",
