        "answer": "To ensure clear documentation and communication of the ulnar nerve injury complication, I would:\n\n**Document in the medical record:**\n- Detailed description of the complication (ulnar nerve injury during elbow arthroscopy)\n- Precise timing of when the injury was identified during the procedure\n- Exact location and nature of the injury (partial vs. complete, compression vs. transection)\n- Immediate management steps taken intraoperatively\n- Assessment of nerve function at the end of the procedure\n- Post-operative examination findings and neurological status\n\n**Operation note:**\n- Include a comprehensive account of the procedure, including the complication\n- Document the technique used, any difficulties encountered, and how the complication was managed\n- Note any additional procedures performed due to the complication\n\n**Team communication:**\n- Verbally handover to recovery and ward staff about the complication and specific monitoring requirements\n- Inform the consultant if not present during the surgery\n- Alert the multidisciplinary team members who will be involved in follow-up care (neurology, hand therapy)\n- Ensure the GP is informed via the discharge summary\n\n**Follow-up plan documentation:**\n- Clearly outline the follow-up plan including:\n  1. Timing of nerve conduction studies\n  2. Referral to hand therapy\n  3. Schedule for outpatient follow-up appointments\n  4. Criteria for urgent review if symptoms worsen\n  5. Rehabilitation protocol\n\n**Incident reporting:**\n- Complete a clinical incident form as per hospital policy\n- Document the incident for discussion at departmental morbidity and mortality meetings\n\n**Patient communication plan:**\n- Document the discussion held with Thomas and his father\n- Record their understanding of the situation and any specific concerns raised\n- Note any written information provided to them\n\nThis comprehensive documentation ensures continuity of care, facilitates appropriate follow-up, meets medico-legal requirements, and supports the duty of candour process.",
