      {
        "answer": "Documentation in a suspected non-accidental injury case must be meticulous, objective, and comprehensive as it may be used in child protection proceedings and potentially court:\n\n**Medical records documentation:**\n\n1. **History:**\n   - Record the history verbatim using quotation marks for direct quotes\n   - Note who provided the history (mother in this case)\n   - Document any changes or inconsistencies in the history\n   - Record the timing of events precisely\n   - Note the mother's demeanor and reactions objectively\n\n2. **Examination findings:**\n   - Document all injuries systematically by body region\n   - Record precise measurements, shapes, and colors of bruises\n   - Note the estimated age of bruises based on appearance\n   - Describe the femur fracture pattern in detail\n   - Document the healing clavicle fracture\n   - Use body diagrams to mark locations of all injuries\n   - Arrange medical photography with appropriate consent\n\n3. **Investigations:**\n   - Document all radiological findings\n   - Record results of skeletal survey\n   - Note any additional investigations (blood tests, etc.)\n\n4. **Assessment:**\n   - Clearly state my concerns regarding NAI\n   - Explain why the injuries are inconsistent with the history provided\n   - Distinguish between factual observations and professional opinions\n   - Avoid definitive statements about abuse (e.g., use 'consistent with NAI' rather than 'definitely NAI')\n\n5. **Actions taken:**\n   - Record all communications with other professionals (consultant, safeguarding lead, social services)\n   - Document the time and content of referrals made\n   - Note discussions with the mother including her responses\n   - Record the plan for admission and further management\n\n**Safeguarding documentation:**\n\n1. Complete a formal safeguarding referral form\n2. Write a detailed medical report if requested\n3. Document attendance at and contributions to strategy meetings\n4. Keep contemporaneous notes of all discussions related to the case\n\n**Timing and security:**\n\n1. All documentation should be completed contemporaneously or as soon as possible\n2. Ensure all records are dated, timed, signed, and my name printed\n3. Follow information governance protocols regarding sensitive information\n\nThis comprehensive documentation provides an objective record that serves the child's best interests and fulfills my professional obligations.",
