ation (usually within 60 minutes of incision) and ensuring VTE (venous thromboembolism) prophylaxis like SCDs or heparin are active.5. Human Factors and CommunicationFlattening the Hierarchy: Encouraging a culture where any team member (nurses, students, anesthetists) feels empowered to speak up if they notice a potential breach in sterility or safety.Briefing and Debriefing: Holding a morning \"huddle\" to discuss the day's cases and any specific equipment needs or patient-specific concerns.",
